\DOC DISCARD_FLAGS_TAC

\TYPE {DISCARD_FLAGS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Deletes from the assumption list those assumptions that describe the value of a
processor condition-flag component in a given state, leaving the conclusion
unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal, it drops every assumption whose
left-hand side is a read of a flag component in some state, keeping all other
assumptions (register and memory reads, arithmetic side conditions,
frame/{MAYCHANGE} facts, the loaded-code fact) in their original relative
order, so the remaining assumptions form a subset {A'} of {A}:
{
         A ?- t
   ===================  DISCARD_FLAGS_TAC
         A' ?- t
}
\noindent The number of assumptions removed varies, and in the observed traces
several flag assumptions are discarded at once; some flag assumptions stated in
other syntactic forms are left in place.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show only this single-subgoal, assumption-pruning
behaviour, on goals arising from x86 machine-state reasoning.

\ENDDOC
